fix: unread flags that no message backs up

Two ways a channel ends up marked unread with nothing to show, leaving the sidebar
unable to say more than "unread, no idea how much".

`unread` is restored from the store as-is. Read the channel from another client and
soju's MARKREAD arrives with the marker already stored, so the recount is skipped and
the stale level survives every reload. Nothing delivered after the read marker means
nothing unread: drop the level and write that back.

History is fetched for the targets that moved since the newest receipt held across all
buffers, and that point can be well past one buffer's own read marker — so a buffer
left unread days ago comes back empty. Fetch the window that is missing, from its read
marker up to where the fetch above started.

⚠️ Which is why those fetches are now awaited and record where they began: a second pass
running alongside them asks for the same window and every line is inserted twice. And
since fetchHistoryBetween() ignores its `before` bound — it asks AFTER and keeps going
until the limit runs out — the upper bound is enforced on the results. Only PRIVMSG and
NOTICE count as already loaded: on a busy channel the newest lines after the marker are
joins and quits, and those mark nothing unread.

Two traps in this code: isReceiptBefore() counts equal times as "before", and equal is
the normal case for a channel read to its end; getReceipt() ignores the type it is
given and always returns the read receipt — fixing that also moves where fetchBacklog
starts from, which is a separate call.

